                       "id":  "ingles-89",
                       "texto_apoio":  "Gene editing techniques now allow scientists to correct mutations responsible for certain hereditary diseases before a child is born. While the medical potential is significant, many researchers urge caution, warning that editing genes passed on to future generations raises ethical questions that society has not yet fully addressed.",
